---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import QualificationNotice from "../components/QualificationNotice.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Healthcare | BeaconGuard for Regulated Healthcare AI Actions"
  description="BeaconGuard independently authorizes AI provider invocation and declared healthcare actions. The AI result remains untrusted; clinical judgment and healthcare systems of record remain authoritative."
>
  <section class="stack-section industry-hero">
    <p class="section-label">HEALTHCARE WORKFLOWS</p>
    <h1>Govern healthcare AI actions before they execute.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      BeaconGuard independently authorizes AI provider invocation and declared
      healthcare actions. The returned AI result remains an untrusted proposal,
      while clinical judgment and healthcare systems of record remain
      authoritative.
    </p>

    <figure class="industry-diagram">
      <img
        src="/images/diagrams/industries/beaconguard-healthcare-governed-ai-transaction.png"
        alt="Healthcare governed AI transaction. A clinical enterprise application prepares a governed request, Request Admission controls whether the AI provider may be invoked, the returned AI result remains untrusted, Result-to-Action controls the intended clinical or operational action, the enterprise application executes only an authorized action, the healthcare system of record remains authoritative, and both authorization decisions produce Verifiable Decision Records."
        width="1536"
        height="512"
        loading="eager"
        decoding="async"
      />
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>The clinical authorization boundary</h2>
    <p>
      Request Admission DENY prevents provider invocation. Result-to-Action DENY
      prevents enterprise effect. Verify remains read-only and cannot grant
      runtime permission.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Authorization scope</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        BeaconGuard authorizes whether the application may invoke the AI
        provider under the Active Verified Release.
      </li>
      <li>
        After an untrusted AI result returns, the application declares the
        intended action. BeaconGuard authorizes or denies that declared action.
      </li>
      <li>
        The enterprise application executes only an authorized action. The EHR
        and other healthcare systems of record remain authoritative.
      </li>
      <li>
        BeaconGuard does not replace the EHR, make clinical determinations, or
        certify model-content correctness.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Existing systems remain in place</h2>
    <p>
      BeaconGuard does not replace the EHR, privacy office, clinical governance,
      care-management platforms, or other systems of record. Customer governance
      retains clinical, privacy, and compliance judgment.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Healthcare action-control scenarios</h2>
    <p>
      Illustrative controlled examples of the same governed pattern: AI proposes,
      the application declares, BeaconGuard authorizes, the application executes,
      and the healthcare system of record remains authoritative.
    </p>
    <div class="scenario-grid">
      <article class="scenario-card scenario-card--lead">
        <p class="section-label">LEAD SCENARIO</p>
        <h3>Send a patient communication</h3>
        <ul class="scenario-flow">
          <li>AI proposes outreach or follow-up messaging.</li>
          <li>The application declares the intended send, queue, or status update.</li>
          <li>BeaconGuard evaluates the active controls.</li>
          <li>ALLOW permits the application to proceed; DENY prevents enterprise effect.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="scenario-authority">
          Care-operations platforms and the EHR remain authoritative.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="scenario-card">
        <h3>Draft clinical documentation</h3>
        <ul class="scenario-flow">
          <li>AI proposes draft documentation text.</li>
          <li>The application declares insert, review, or documentation-state update.</li>
          <li>BeaconGuard evaluates the active controls.</li>
          <li>ALLOW permits the declared use of the draft; DENY prevents enterprise effect.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="scenario-authority">
          The EHR and clinical documentation systems remain authoritative.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="scenario-card">
        <h3>Route a care-operations task</h3>
        <ul class="scenario-flow">
          <li>AI proposes a summary or routing recommendation.</li>
          <li>The application declares the intended route, status, or follow-up task.</li>
          <li>BeaconGuard evaluates the active controls.</li>
          <li>ALLOW permits the application to proceed; DENY hard-stops enterprise effect.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="scenario-authority">
          Care-management platforms and the EHR remain authoritative.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>What BeaconGuard does not claim</h2>
    <ul class="bg-nonclaim-list">
      <li>Clinical correctness or medical certification of AI output</li>
      <li>Replacement of clinician judgment or privacy-office decisions</li>
      <li>Replacement of the EHR or other systems of record</li>
      <li>Independent HIPAA certification or legal compliance attestation</li>
      <li>Customer healthcare production validation or production-ready status</li>
      <li>Authorization of model content as semantic truth</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <QualificationNotice variant="full" />

  <section class="stack-section">
    <div class="page-actions">
      <a
        class="btn-primary"
        href="mailto:architecture@beaconguardassurance.com?subject=Healthcare%20Workflow%20Review"
      >
        Request a Healthcare Workflow Review
      </a>
      <a class="btn-secondary" href="/canonical-workflow">Review Governed Transaction</a>
      <a class="btn-secondary" href="/docs/architecture">Review System Architecture</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
